Why: platform-windows passes its own clippy with `-D warnings`: clippy's machine-applicable suggestions, `# Safety` docs on two unsafe scroll functions, a type alias, a test-only `cfg` on a helper only tests call, a removed unused duplicate of `tools::build_registry`, and scoped allows (four upstream signatures with eight arguments, and one comparison that keeps its lossy UTF-16 decode to match how the field value was read). Behaviour is unchanged.

